DRAFT — FOR ANDY VACA / GRY HAT CYBERSECURITY LLC TO REVIEW
================================================================

This file is a placeholder tester end-user license. It is not a finished
agreement. Do not give it to a paying customer, and do not describe it as
counsel-reviewed, until Andy has replaced this banner with a version he
is willing to stand behind.

Until that happens, the operative points for an insider tester are the
ones below. Where this draft is silent or clumsy, ask andy@gryhat.com
before you assume a right.

Citadel Audit — Insider Tester Evaluation Terms (draft)
-------------------------------------------------------

Product. "Citadel Audit" (application name "Citadel Cyber Guardian") is
proprietary software of GRY HAT CYBERSECURITY LLC ("GRYHAT"). All rights
not expressly granted in a countersigned license, or in a license key
GRYHAT actually issues to you, are reserved.

Who these terms cover. They cover an insider tester who receives a build
from the public download repository or from a GitHub Release, and a
machine-bound evaluation key. They are not the commercial subscription,
the partner-seat terms, or a customer statement of work.

Grant. GRYHAT grants you a limited, revocable, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to install and run the tester
build on the computer whose Machine ID you submitted, for internal
evaluation, for as long as the key says it is valid.

What you do not receive.

- No right to redistribute the build, post the binary elsewhere, or
  share a license key.
- No right to rent, host, or white-label the app.
- No ownership of the software, the signatures, the mappings, or the
  model weights bundled with a build.
- No right to remove proprietary notices.

Machine binding. A key is checked on the machine. It is not a floating
seat and it does not call a license server. Bypassing that check is
outside this grant.

Your networks. You may scan only a range that the owner of that network
has authorized you to scan. You are responsible for that authorization.
Do not put client addresses, hostnames, evidence files, or license keys
into a public GitHub issue.

Feedback. You may send bug reports and suggestions. GRYHAT may use that
feedback without obligation to you. Do not send it if a third party owns
it and you cannot share it.

Tester builds are unfinished. macOS and Linux builds have been run on
real hardware. Windows builds are an experimental preview and are
untested. A tester build may be unsigned. Gatekeeper or SmartScreen
warnings on an unsigned file are expected. There is no uptime commitment
and no support level in this draft beyond answers Andy chooses to give.

No warranty. THE TESTER BUILD IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE."
TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, GRYHAT DISCLAIMS WARRANTIES OF
MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND
NON-INFRINGEMENT. CITADEL AUDIT DOES NOT CERTIFY YOU AGAINST CMMC,
NIST SP 800-171, SOC 2, PCI-DSS, HIPAA, GDPR, THE EU AI ACT, ISO 27001,
ISO 42001, OR IAiGACB. MAPPINGS ARE EVIDENCE. THEY ARE NOT AN ATTESTATION.
WHERE IAiGACB IS NAMED, THE WORD IS "ALIGNED WITH." THIS DRAFT DOES NOT GRANT OR CLAIM AN IAiGACB CREDENTIAL.

Liability. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, GRYHAT WILL NOT BE
LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR LOST-PROFIT
DAMAGES, OR FOR A CLIENT'S RELIANCE ON A TESTER BUILD. The cap, the
governing law, and the venue are intentionally left blank in this draft
for counsel. Do not invent them. Placeholder only, not a choice: the
company operates from California.

Stop. GRYHAT may end an evaluation key at expiry or by telling you to
stop. When it ends, delete the tester build from machines you control,
except for evidence files a client engagement already requires you to
keep. Those evidence files are the client's records, not a license to
keep using the app.

Contact. andy@gryhat.com

